  "tldr": {
   "model": "tldr@v2.0.0",
   "text": "This study failed to demonstrate the expected linear relationship between ETT cuff pressures and the maximum altitude achieved during typical air-medical transportation in this system, and at altitudes less than 3,000 feet above sea level the effect of altitude change on ETT pressure is minimal and does not require a change in practice to saline-filled cuffs."
  },
